[2026-01-30T14:57:36.227Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HhHsZ16jcxPusqMPdv6zgQ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation: Add compile-time finding type validation to catch mismatches between config and report methods\n     2→\n     3→## Context Area\n     4→Research Templates\n     5→\n     6→## Description\n     7→Add compile-time finding type validation to catch mismatches between config and report methods\n     8→\n     9→## Implementation Details\n    10→\n    11→## Vision\n    12→Implement type-safe finding type validation that catches mismatches between template configuration (finding_types in TemplateConfig) and report generation methods at development time rather than runtime.\n    13→\n    14→## Business Value\n    15→- Prevents silent bugs where report methods reference non-existent finding types\n    16→- Catches typos in finding_type strings across 11 templates with 6-12 types each\n    17→- Improves IDE autocomplete and developer experience\n    18→- Reduces debugging time for template authors\n    19→\n    20→## Scope\n    21→**Included:**\n    22→- Create FindingType enum per template for type-safe references\n    23→- Add validation decorator to verify finding types in methods match config\n    24→- Runtime validation during template initialization\n    25→- Unit tests for validation\n    26→\n    27→**Excluded:**\n    28→- Changing the finding_type storage format in results/database\n    29→- Modifying the extraction or search systems\n    30→\n    31→## Key Components\n    32→1. `FindingType` enum base class with validation helper methods\n    33→2. Template-specific enums (e.g., DueDiligenceFindingType, FinancialFindingType)\n    34→3. `@validates_finding_types` decorator for report methods\n    35→4. Template.__init__ validation hook\n    36→\n    37→## Technical Approach\n    38→1. Define base protocol for FindingType enums with string conversion\n    39→2. Generate enums from existing FindingTypeConfig lists:\n    40→   ```python\n    41→   class DueDiligenceFindingType(str, Enum):\n    42→       COMPANY_PROFILE = \"company_profile\"\n    43→       FINANCIAL_HEALTH = \"financial_health\"\n    44→       LEGAL_HISTORY = \"legal_history\"\n    45→       RED_FLAG = \"red_flag\"\n    46→       # ...\n    47→   ```\n    48→3. Create validator that scans method source for finding_type references\n    49→4. Run validation in BaseTemplate.__init_subclass__ hook\n    50→\n    51→## Files to Modify\n    52→- `actor/src/templates/base.py` - Add FindingType protocol and validation decorator\n    53→- `actor/src/templates/due_diligence.py` - Add enum, use in report methods\n    54→- `actor/src/templates/financial.py` - Add enum, use in report methods\n    55→- All other template files\n    56→\n    57→## Success Criteria\n    58→- [ ] All templates have FindingType enums matching their config\n    59→- [ ] Typos in finding_type strings cause test/init failures\n    60→- [ ] IDE provides autocomplete for finding types\n    61→- [ ] No runtime behavior changes\n    62→\n    63→## Potential Challenges\n    64→- Backwards compatibility with string-based lookups - solved by making enum inherit from str\n    65→- Performance of source code scanning - mitigate by caching, only run in debug mode\n    66→- Dynamic finding types in some edge cases - allow explicit opt-out\n    67→\n    68→## Instructions\n    69→\n    70→1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n    71→2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n    72→3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n    73→4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n    74→5. Test the changes work as expected\n    75→\n    76→## Notes\n    77→\n    78→This requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\n    79→Focus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n    80→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"063d9692-0974-4418-8890-3933b0ef315a","uuid":"1e8a2066-52eb-4e36-8102-bccfdb334f6f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\dir-1769783006887-add-compile-time-finding-type-validation.md","content":"# Implementation: Add compile-time finding type validation to catch mismatches between config and report methods\n\n## Context Area\nResearch Templates\n\n## Description\nAdd compile-time finding type validation to catch mismatches between config and report methods\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Vision\nImplement type-safe finding type validation that catches mismatches between template configuration (finding_types in TemplateConfig) and report generation methods at development time rather than runtime.\n\n## Business Value\n- Prevents silent bugs where report methods reference non-existent finding types\n- Catches typos in finding_type strings across 11 templates with 6-12 types each\n- Improves IDE autocomplete and developer experience\n- Reduces debugging time for template authors\n\n## Scope\n**Included:**\n- Create FindingType enum per template for type-safe references\n- Add validation decorator to verify finding types in methods match config\n- Runtime validation during template initialization\n- Unit tests for validation\n\n**Excluded:**\n- Changing the finding_type storage format in results/database\n- Modifying the extraction or search systems\n\n## Key Components\n1. `FindingType` enum base class with validation helper methods\n2. Template-specific enums (e.g., DueDiligenceFindingType, FinancialFindingType)\n3. `@validates_finding_types` decorator for report methods\n4. Template.__init__ validation hook\n\n## Technical Approach\n1. Define base protocol for FindingType enums with string conversion\n2. Generate enums from existing FindingTypeConfig lists:\n   ```python\n   class DueDiligenceFindingType(str, Enum):\n       COMPANY_PROFILE = \"company_profile\"\n       FINANCIAL_HEALTH = \"financial_health\"\n       LEGAL_HISTORY = \"legal_history\"\n       RED_FLAG = \"red_flag\"\n       # ...\n   ```\n3. Create validator that scans method source for finding_type references\n4. Run validation in BaseTemplate.__init_subclass__ hook\n\n## Files to Modify\n- `actor/src/templates/base.py` - Add FindingType protocol and validation decorator\n- `actor/src/templates/due_diligence.py` - Add enum, use in report methods\n- `actor/src/templates/financial.py` - Add enum, use in report methods\n- All other template files\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] All templates have FindingType enums matching their config\n- [ ] Typos in finding_type strings cause test/init failures\n- [ ] IDE provides autocomplete for finding types\n- [ ] No runtime behavior changes\n\n## Potential Challenges\n- Backwards compatibility with string-based lookups - solved by making enum inherit from str\n- Performance of source code scanning - mitigate by caching, only run in debug mode\n- Dynamic finding types in some edge cases - allow explicit opt-out\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":80}}}
