 media presence and engagement\",\n    46→                \"Professional profiles (LinkedIn, industry directories)\",\n    47→            ]\n    48→        },\n    49→        {\n    50→            \"name\": \"INDUSTRY REPUTATION\",\n    51→            \"items\": [\n    52→                \"Industry association membership\",\n    53→                \"Awards, certifications\",\n    54→                \"Peer recognition\",\n    55→            ]\n    56→        },\n    57→        {\n    58→            \"name\": \"NEWS & MEDIA\",\n    59→            \"items\": [\n    60→                \"News coverage (positive and negative)\",\n    61→                \"Investigations or exposés\",\n    62→                \"Press releases vs. independent coverage\",\n    63→            ]\n    64→        },\n    65→    ],\n    66→    search_depth_guidance={\n    67→        \"quick\": \"Focus on 3-4 angles (scam reports, reviews, legitimacy)\",\n    68→        \"standard\": \"Cover 5-6 angles\",\n    69→        \"deep\": \"Comprehensive coverage\",\n    70→    },\n    71→\n    72→    extraction_intro=\"You are a consumer protection analyst checking if an entity is trustworthy.\",\n    73→    finding_types=[\n    74→        FindingTypeConfig(\n    75→            name=\"trust_signal\",\n    76→            display_name=\"Trust Signal\",\n    77→            description=\"Positive indicators of legitimacy. Must be verifiable, not self-reported.\",\n    78→            extracted_data_schema='{\"signal_type\": \"\", \"verification_status\": \"verified/unverified/self_reported\", \"source\": \"\", \"strength\": \"strong/moderate/weak\"}',\n    79→            analysis_fallback=\"This trust signal provides evidence of legitimacy that can be verified.\",\n    80→        ),\n    81→        FindingTypeConfig(\n    82→            name=\"warning_sign\",\n    83→            display_name=\"Warning Sign\",\n    84→            description=\"Red flags and concerns. Be specific about what's concerning and why.\",\n    85→            extracted_data_schema='{\"warning_type\": \"\", \"severity\": \"critical/significant/minor\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"recommendation\": \"\"}',\n    86→            analysis_fallback=\"This warning sign warrants caution and further investigation.\",\n    87→        ),\n    88→        FindingTypeConfig(\n    89→            name=\"complaint_pattern\",\n    90→            display_name=\"Complaint Pattern\",\n    91→            description=\"Recurring issues reported by multiple people\",\n    92→            extracted_data_schema='{\"complaint_type\": \"\", \"frequency\": \"many/several/few\", \"resolution\": \"resolved/unresolved/mixed\", \"sources\": []}',\n    93→            analysis_fallback=\"This complaint pattern indicates systemic issues that affect multiple customers.\",\n    94→        ),\n    95→        FindingTypeConfig(\n    96→            name=\"verification_status\",\n    97→            display_name=\"Verification Status\",\n    98→            description=\"Credentials, licenses, certifications\",\n    99→            extracted_data_schema='{\"credential\": \"\", \"issuer\": \"\", \"status\": \"valid/expired/unverifiable/fake\", \"verification_url\": \"\"}',\n   100→            analysis_fallback=\"This verification status helps establish whether claims are legitimate.\",\n   101→        ),\n   102→        FindingTypeConfig(\n   103→            name=\"sentiment_trend\",\n   104→            display_name=\"Sentiment Trend\",\n   105→            description=\"How perception has changed over time\",\n   106→            extracted_data_schema='{\"direction\": \"improving/declining/stable\", \"timeframe\": \"\", \"key_events\": [], \"current_sentiment\": \"positive/negative/mixed\"}',\n   107→            analysis_fallback=\"This sentiment trend indicates how the entity's reputation has evolved.\",\n   108→        ),\n   109→        FindingTypeConfig(\n   110→            name=\"comparison_benchmark\",\n   111→            display_name=\"Comparison Benchmark\",\n   112→            description=\"How they compare to similar entities\",\n   113→            extracted_data_schema='{\"benchmark\": \"\", \"rating\": \"above_average/average/below_average\", \"comparison_basis\": \"\"}',\n   114→            analysis_fallback=\"This comparison helps contextualize the entity's performance relative to peers.\",\n   115→        ),\n   116→    ],\n   117→    analysis_instruction=\"\"\"YOUR EXPERT REPUTATION ANALYSIS (REQUIRED - 2-4 sentences) explaining:\n   118→  * WHY this signal matters for assessing trustworthiness\n   119→  * What this PATTERN indicates about the entity's practices\n   120→  * How this COMPARES to typical behavior of legitimate vs problematic actors\n   121→  * What SPECIFIC RISKS or assurances this provides\"\"\",\n   122→    extraction_guidelines=\"\"\"CRITICAL: The \"analysis\" field must provide substantive assessment reasoning, not just describe the finding.\n   123→Good example: \"This pattern of unresolved complaints is a major red flag because legitimate companies typically respond to BBB complaints within 14 days. The consistent theme of delayed refunds suggests systemic cash flow issues or intentional delay tactics. Companies with this complaint volume and non-response rate have a 78% correlation with eventual enforcement action.\"\n   124→\n   125→IMPORTANT:\n   126→- WARNING SIGNS are the most important - surface these first\n   127→- Be skeptical of self-reported credentials\n   128→- Note if reviews appear fake or manipulated\n   129→- Distinguish between isolated incidents and patterns\"\"\",\n   130→\n   131→    priority_finding_types=[\"warning_sign\", \"complaint_pattern\", \"verification_status\", \"trust_signal\", \"sentiment_trend\", \"comparison_benchmark\"],\n   132→    grouping_order=[\"warning_sign\", \"complaint_pattern\", \"trust_signal\", \"verification_status\", \"sentiment_trend\", \"comparison_benchmark\"],\n   133→)\n   134→\n   135→\n   136→class ReputationTemplate(BaseTemplate):\n   137→    \"\"\"Template for reputation and legitimacy checks.\n   138→\n   139→    Helps users verify whether a business, service, or professional\n   140→    is legitimate and trustworthy before engaging with them.\n   141→    \"\"\"\n   142→\n   143→    template_id = \"reputation\"\n   144→    template_name = \"Reputation Check\"\n   145→    description = \"Verify legitimacy and trustworthiness - scam detection, reviews, and trust signals\"\n   146→\n   147→    # Data-driven configuration\n   148→    config = REPUTATION_CONFIG\n   149→\n   150→    # Report hints for component-based rendering\n   151→    report_hints = ReportHints(\n   152→        template_type=\"reputation\",\n   153→        structure=\"verdict_first\",\n   154→        findings_grouping=\"sentiment\",\n   155→        tone=\"advisory\",\n   156→        decision_format=\"checklist\",\n   157→        emphasis=[\"trust_score\", \"red_flags\", \"user_sentiment\", \"verification\"],\n   158→        required_components=[\n   159→            ComponentType.TRUST_DASHBOARD,\n   160→            ComponentType.CHECKLIST,\n   161→            ComponentType.FINDINGS_TABLE,\n   162→        ],\n   163→        optional_components=[\n   164→            ComponentType.QUOTE_CAROUSEL,\n   165→            ComponentType.TIMELINE,\n   166→            ComponentType.KEY_INSIGHTS,\n   167→            ComponentType.SOURCE_LIST,\n   168→        ],\n   169→        visualization_preference=[\"trust_gauge\", \"sentiment_chart\", \"verification_checklist\"],\n   170→        custom_sections={\n   171→            \"trust_score_prominent\": True,\n   172→            \"red_flag_alerts\": True,\n   173→            \"sentiment_breakdown\": True,\n   174→        }\n   175→    )\n   176→\n   177→    # Expert perspectives for reputation checks\n   178→    default_perspectives = [\n   179→        \"consumer_protection\",   # Scam detection focus\n   180→        \"reputation_analyst\",    # Pattern analysis\n   181→        \"fact_checker\",          # Verification specialist\n   182→        \"industry_benchmarker\",  # Comparative assessment\n   183→    ]\n   184→\n   185→    default_max_searches = 6\n   186→\n   187→    # Reputation checks need thorough bias detection (fake reviews are common)\n   188→    verification_config = {\n   189→        \"cross_reference\": \"thorough\",\n   190→        \"bias_detection\": \"thorough\",\n   191→        \"expert_sanity_check\": \"standard\",\n   192→        \"source_quality\": \"thorough\",\n   193→    }\n   194→\n   195→    def get_supported_report_variants(self) -> List[str]:\n   196→        \"\"\"Reputation check supports trust_report variant.\"\"\"\n   197→        return [\"full_report\", \"executive_summary\", \"trust_report\"]\n   198→\n   199→    def generate_trust_report(\n   200→        self,\n   201→        result: Dict[str, Any],\n   202→        title: Optional[str] = None,\n   203→    ) -> str:\n   204→        \"\"\"Generate trust-focused report.\"\"\"\n   205→        query = result.get(\"query\", \"Unknown\")\n   206→        report_title = title or f\"Reputation Check: {query[:50]}\"\n   207→\n   208→        sections = []\n   209→        sections.append(f\"# {report_title}\")\n   210→        sections.append(\"\")\n   211→        sections.append(f\"**Subject:** {query}\")\n   212→        sections.append(f\"**Date:** {datetime.now().strftime('%B %d, %Y')}\")\n   213→        sections.append(\"\")\n   214→\n   215→        findings = result.get(\"findings\", [])\n   216→\n   217→        # Trust verdict\n   218→        warnings = [f for f in findings if f.get(\"finding_type\") == \"warning_sign\"]\n   219→        critical_warnings = [f for f in warnings\n   220→                           if f.get(\"extracted_data\", {}).get(\"severity\") == \"critical\"]\n   221→        trust_signals = [f for f in findings if f.get(\"finding_type\") == \"trust_signal\"]\n   222→        strong_signals = [f for f in trust_signals\n   223→                        if f.get(\"extracted_data\", {}).get(\"strength\") == \"strong\"]\n   224→\n   225→        sections.append(\"## Trust Verdict\")\n   226→        sections.append(\"\")\n   227→        if critical_warnings:\n   228→            sections.append(\"**DO NOT ENGAGE** - Critical warning signs detected\")\n   229→        elif len(warnings) > len(strong_signals):\n   230→            sections.append(\"**PROCEED WITH CAUTION** - More concerns than trust signals\")\n   231→        elif strong_signals and not warnings:\n   232→            sections.append(\"**APPEARS LEGITIMATE** - Strong trust signals, no warnings\")\n   233→        elif trust_signals and not critical_warnings:\n   234→            sections.append(\"**LIKELY LEGITIMATE** - Some trust signals, minor or no concerns\")\n   235→        else:\n   236→            sections.append(\"**INSUFFICIENT DATA** - Unable to verify, proceed carefully\")\n   237→        sections.append(\"\")\n   238→\n   239→        # Warning signs\n   240→        if warnings:\n   241→            sections.append(\"## Warning Signs\")\n   242→            sections.append(\"\")\n   243→            for w in warnings[:6]:\n   244→                extracted = w.get(\"extracted_data\", {})\n   245→                severity = extracted.get(\"severity\", \"\").upper() if extracted else \"\"\n   246→                prefix = f\"**[{severity}]** \" if severity else \"\"\n   247→                sections.append(f\"- {prefix}{w.get('summary', w.get('content', '')[:100])}\")\n   248→            sections.append(\"\")\n   249→\n   250→        # Complaint patterns\n   251→        complaints = [f for f in findings if f.get(\"finding_type\") == \"complaint_pattern\"]\n   252→        if complaints:\n   253→            sections.append(\"## Complaint Patterns\")\n   254→            sections.append(\"\")\n   255→            for c in complaints[:4]:\n   256→                sections.append(f\"- {c.get('summary', c.get('content', '')[:100])}\")\n   257→            sections.append(\"\")\n   258→\n   259→        # Trust signals\n   260→        if trust_signals:\n   261→            sections.append(\"## Trust Signals\")\n   262→            sections.append(\"\")\n   263→            for t in trust_signals[:5]:\n   264→                extracted = t.get(\"extracted_data\", {})\n   265→                strength = extracted.get(\"strength\", \"\").upper() if extracted else \"\"\n   266→                prefix = f\"**[{strength}]** \" if strength else \"\"\n   267→                sections.append(f\"- {prefix}{t.get('summary', t.get('content', '')[:100])}\")\n   268→            sections.append(\"\")\n   269→\n   270→        # Verification status\n   271→        verifications = [f for f in findings if f.get(\"finding_type\") == \"verification_status\"]\n   272→        if verifications:\n   273→            sections.append(\"## Verification Status\")\n   274→            sections.append(\"\")\n   275→            for v in verifications[:4]:\n   276→                extracted = v.get(\"extracted_data\", {})\n   277→                status = extracted.get(\"status\", \"\").upper() if extracted else \"\"\n   278→                credential = extracted.get(\"credential\", \"\") if extracted else \"\"\n   279→                if credential and status:\n   280→                    sections.append(f\"- **{credential}**: {status}\")\n   281→                else:\n   282→                    sections.append(f\"- {v.get('summary', v.get('content', '')[:100])}\")\n   283→            sections.append(\"\")\n   284→\n   285→        return \"\\n\".join(sections)\n   286→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"063d9692-0974-4418-88