t use finding types.\"\"\"\n         method._uses_finding_types = True\n         return method\n     ```\n\n   - `actor/src/templates/due_diligence.py` - Finding types: company_profile, financial_health, legal_history, red_flag, reputation_signal, key_person\n   \n   - `actor/src/templates/financial.py` - Finding types: bullish_signal, bearish_signal, risk, red_flag, financial_metric, prediction\n   \n   - `actor/src/templates/investigative.py` - Finding types: actor, event, relationship, financial, evidence, pattern, gap\n   \n   - `actor/src/templates/reputation.py` - Finding types: trust_signal, warning_sign, complaint_pattern, verification_status, sentiment_trend, comparison_benchmark\n   \n   - `actor/src/templates/purchase_decision.py` - Finding types: product_strength, product_weakness, real_user_experience, hidden_cost, alternative_option, value_assessment\n   \n   - `actor/src/templates/understanding.py` - Finding types: event_chain, media_narrative, financial_motivation, misinformation_pattern, source_credibility, actor_interest, counter_narrative, historical_parallel\n   \n   - `actor/src/templates/legal.py` - Finding types: evidence, fact, event, claim, pattern\n   \n   - `actor/src/templates/contract.py` - Finding types: contract_entity, contract_terms, pricing_analysis, bid_process, suspicious_element, connected_entity\n   \n   - `actor/src/templates/competitive.py` - Finding types: fact, actor, event, relationship, evidence, pattern\n   \n   - `actor/src/templates/tech_market.py` - Finding types: tech_trend, market_trend, adoption_pattern, financial_metric, prediction, red_flag\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet in the current task\n   - Previous tasks: TypeScript/playwright errors were pre-existing and resolved by excluding playwright files from tsconfig.json\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Analyzed all 11 template files to catalog their finding types\n   - Designed validation system that scans Python source code for finding_type references\n   - Created enum base class that inherits from str for seamless JSON compatibility\n   - Added validation function that checks priority_finding_types and grouping_order against configured types\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: dir-1769783005762-unify-animation-utilities-into-shared\"\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: dir-1769783006887-add-compile-time-finding-type-validation\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Add `__init_subclass__` hook to BaseTemplate class for automatic validation\n   - Create FindingType enums for each template (DueDiligenceFindingType, FinancialFindingType, etc.)\n   - Update template config to use enums instead of raw strings\n   - Verify Python syntax and test validation\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Working on requirement: \"Add compile-time finding type validation to catch mismatches between config and report methods\"\n   \n   Just added to `actor/src/templates/base.py`:\n   - `FindingType(str, Enum)` base class with `values()`, `from_string()`, `is_valid()` methods\n   - `validate_finding_types()` function that scans template methods for finding_type references\n   - `validates_finding_types` decorator for marking methods\n\n   Current location in base.py: Line 192, at the BaseTemplate class definition. Need to add `__init_subclass__` hook.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Add the `__init_subclass__` hook to BaseTemplate class to automatically run validation when subclasses are defined. This was the next planned step in the todo list:\n   - \"[pending] Add __init_subclass__ validation hook to BaseTemplate\"\n   \n   The hook should call `validate_finding_types()` and either warn or raise errors for mismatches.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\mkdol\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-mkdol-dolla-res\\063d9692-0974-4418-8890-3933b0ef315a.jsonl\nPlease continue the conversation from where