[2026-01-30T15:04:52.318Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01J1M8yQAV1pEk6a2uyFZ8My","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've completed the implementation of compile-time finding type validation for Python templates. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Summary\n\n### 1. `actor/src/templates/base.py` - Core validation infrastructure:\n- **`FindingType(str, Enum)`** - Base class for template-specific finding type enums that inherits from `str` for JSON compatibility\n  - `values()` - Get all valid finding type values as strings\n  - `from_string()` - Convert string to enum member with validation\n  - `is_valid()` - Check if a string is a valid finding type\n\n- **`validate_finding_types()`** - Function that scans template method source code for finding_type references and compares against configured types\n\n- **`validates_finding_types`** - Decorator to mark methods that use finding types (for documentation)\n\n- **`BaseTemplate.__init_subclass__`** - Hook that runs validation when template subclasses are defined, issuing warnings for mismatches\n\n### 2. FindingType enums added to all 10 templates:\n- `DueDiligenceFindingType` - company_profile, financial_health, legal_history, red_flag, reputation_signal, key_person\n- `FinancialFindingType` - bullish_signal, bearish_signal, risk, red_flag, financial_metric, prediction\n- `InvestigativeFindingType` - actor, event, relationship, financial, evidence, pattern, gap\n- `ReputationFindingType` - trust_signal, warning_sign, complaint_pattern, verification_status, sentiment_trend, comparison_benchmark\n- `PurchaseDecisionFindingType` - product_strength, product_weakness, real_user_experience, hidden_cost, alternative_option, value_assessment\n- `UnderstandingFindingType` - event_chain, media_narrative, financial_motivation, misinformation_pattern, source_credibility, actor_interest, counter_narrative, historical_parallel\n- `LegalF